  "problem": "Let $f(x)$ be the $2$-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=-4x$ defined on $[-1,1).$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of a series converging to the $2$-periodic extension of \n\n$$\nG(x)=-2{x}^{2}={\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$The Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n-4x\u223c{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}} \non $R,$ we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n-2{x}^{2}\u223c{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-3}}\\cdot {{field-4}}.\n$$",
